                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "39c43689-f755-4ebf-8927-044253a5cab3",
                        "entry_id": "19a204b9-1b2b-3f66-a66b-d129ae8efca3",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "развали́вшись"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f3f0f402-77b7-33cb-98bc-ab67ccbc4228",
                        "entry_id": "19a204b9-1b2b-3f66-a66b-d129ae8efca3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "рассы́паться, утратить цельность, перестать быть собранным вместе или сложенным в порядке; распасться на части, на куски, превратиться в развалины"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cda33b62-0ad6-3a06-9c93-bddfffd58d96",
                        "entry_id": "19a204b9-1b2b-3f66-a66b-d129ae8efca3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. прийти в расстройство, в упадок"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a28f1e2d-36a1-3f18-a194-4c38a41e24c8",
                        "entry_id": "19a204b9-1b2b-3f66-a66b-d129ae8efca3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. лечь, вытянувшись, или сесть в небрежной позе, широко раскинувшись"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4afde258-d3c4-420c-acc6-00c44398c414",
                                "sense_id": "a28f1e2d-36a1-3f18-a194-4c38a41e24c8",
                                "text": "…просто прошёл к его столу, положил перед ним свою папку, а сам сел в довольно удобное полукресло. Меня вдруг двинуло в противоположность, захотелось вдруг развалиться и ногу перекинуть через ногу, и, рассеянно озираясь по сторонам, изрыгнуть какую-нибудь фривольную банальность, вроде: «А ничего себе живут учёные, лихо устроились!»"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dfbe66a9-8116-42ac-a3b9-18049c7ba257",
                        "source_entry_id": "19a204b9-1b2b-3f66-a66b-d129ae8efca3",
                        "target_lang_word": "fall apart",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fall apart",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1662911e-5335-37c8-b893-db6e677f513a",
                                        "entry_id": "9dc226d6-4c48-38ac-9558-70eea620b935",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disintegrate, to break into pieces."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb90c0ef-1f26-4671-be35-e026a7dec524",
                                                "sense_id": "1662911e-5335-37c8-b893-db6e677f513a",
                                                "text": "My old briefcase is falling apart. I'll have to buy a new one."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac177618-568c-4867-b627-fd5a7cad7388",
                                                "sense_id": "1662911e-5335-37c8-b893-db6e677f513a",
                                                "text": "England's World Cup dreams fell apart under a French onslaught on a night when their shortcomings were brutally exposed at the quarter-final stage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c856ca2-eaa5-472b-9007-bea5cc6c5276",
                                                "sense_id": "1662911e-5335-37c8-b893-db6e677f513a",
                                                "text": "It investigated extensive damage caused by a Robeston-Westerleigh train after the brake system under one of its wagons fell apart on October 30 2017."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4681a08-e17b-300b-9b4a-e8effc7975f9",
                                        "entry_id": "9dc226d6-4c48-38ac-9558-70eea620b935",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be emotionally in crisis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10e78b29-b417-4bfb-8096-746e191349a3",
                                                "sense_id": "d4681a08-e17b-300b-9b4a-e8effc7975f9",
                                                "text": "As a result of being addicted to heroin, she was falling apart."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbdf6e2c-11df-4513-8d40-461f3f3439bc",
                                                "sense_id": "d4681a08-e17b-300b-9b4a-e8effc7975f9",
                                                "text": "At first I used to look at so many of us having fights or crying or staggering around messed up somehow and think, \"God, are we fucked up!\" but now what I think is that it was a safe place to fall apart in — one of the few. You didn't have to be politically correct or well-behaved; you could be wild or angry or miserable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ebdf85b6-8f54-3842-8e58-b17bcd9c64fe",
                                        "entry_id": "9dc226d6-4c48-38ac-9558-70eea620b935",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To separate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36bbce16-91af-41af-81a8-f544883552fc",
                                                "sense_id": "ebdf85b6-8f54-3842-8e58-b17bcd9c64fe",
                                                "text": "And when my care was moſt, by Gods pꝛouidence onely, by the burning aſunder of our ſpꝛitſaile-yard with ropes and ſaile, and the ropes about the ſpꝛitſaile-yard of the Carack, whereby we were faſt intangled, we fell apart, with burning of ſome of our ſailes which we had then on booꝛd."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f26587a-ef64-4ca3-8cf1-db5c3fb1e906",
                                                "sense_id": "ebdf85b6-8f54-3842-8e58-b17bcd9c64fe",
                                                "text": "Again the mountains fall apart, and in a wide basin of corn-land and pasture lies the bourgade of La Thuile."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5fee711-49ea-434d-86bf-5683eefee6ca",
                                                "sense_id": "ebdf85b6-8f54-3842-8e58-b17bcd9c64fe",
                                                "text": "You'll say, we've got nothing in common\nNo common ground to start from\nAnd we're falling apart"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07dfa40b-99a4-4930-9db2-b2c3755c89f9",
                                                "sense_id": "ebdf85b6-8f54-3842-8e58-b17bcd9c64fe",
                                                "text": "Others come on behind relentlessly and, in this way, it arrives before me as a tumbleweed of moving birds. Occasionally two of them, newly vanished, suddenly pop back up, all legs and squabbling beak, then they fall apart and resume the stab-and-prise feeding technique that scientists call Zirkeln."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
